<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 9.946 percent on Wednesday from 9.963 percent at the previous auction on March 3.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt had asked for 800 million pounds and accepted bids for 872.950 million, rejecting bids for 110 million. Bills worth 841.800 million mature on Thursday.</p>
<p>The central bank announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: June 12, 1997 (June 5, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 9.946 percent (9.963)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 872.950 million (870.450 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 982.950 million (959.725 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.390-10.074 percent (9.501-10.027)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.390-10.099 percent (9.501-10.099)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 154 (161)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 157 (169)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1/</p>
</text>
